\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1.\cf0  Sing praises you all to our God
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 who call themselves Christians.
\par He opened up his kingdom
\par and sacrificed His son.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. He from his father's own embrace
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 became a little babe,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\qj He who was laid naked in the
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 manger in a stable.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  3. He denied himself his glory
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 to become a poor man
\par He, who was with the creator
\par chose to be a servant.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4.   Caressed in his mother's own arms
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0  he sucked his mother's breast
\par  He who angels keep ceaseless praise
\par  became David's foliage.
\par \pard\li405\sl190\slmult0 
\par \pard\fi-225\li405\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. He who is God himself, took on
\par \pard\li405\sl190\slmult0 our blood and our own flesh,
\par and rather gave us God's image
\par to be worn by us all.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li405\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. He came a servant to us all
\par \pard\li405\sl190\slmult0 and I was raised so high.
\par Do you know someone better than
\par your own love Jesus Christ.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li405\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 7\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 7. The heaven's  gate is open wide
\par \pard\li405\sl190\slmult0 and that of  Paradise,
\par and cherub allows you to go
\par \pard      Praise God oh! praise His name.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2 
\par }

